OL,3,GNEWSAThousands watch centuries-old Lord
OL,4,AMayor's show
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe City of London was taken over by
OL,7,Fone of Britain's oldest traditions as
OL,8,Fthe annual Lord Mayor's Show took
OL,9,Fplace.
OL,11,FDating back more than 800 years, the
OL,12,Fevent marks the appointment of the new
OL,13,FLord Mayor of London, with Alderman
OL,14,FBronek Masojada taking up the position
OL,15,Fthis year.
OL,17,FAbout 6,500 people, 250 horses and more
OL,18,Fthan 50 floats, including a replica of
OL,19,FTower Bridge with rising bascules -
OL,20,Fmovable sections of road - took part.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,324,320,200,140,0,100
